# Strangers (docs/DIALOGUE.md, "Strangers"): the errands' passers-by (docs/ERRANDS.md, "Strangers").
# Their ask stays theirs: its ways are the hub's verbs, paid by the errand rules. These topics are who
# they are and why they're here, in their own words: {their:town}, {their:house}... are the routine's
# own texts. Nobody leans on a stranger through talk. Small means small: a pinch, not a tragedy.
# Lines are spoken by the stranger; someone else in the scene speaks under their own label (say (...)).

conv stranger.any.where
for stranger
topic "Where are you headed?"
prio flavour
once
voice plain

node start
  say Wherever's still standing. I'll know it when I see it, I expect. There used to be a bus along this road. I keep looking up when I hear an engine.
  say You've a look about you, like you know where the houses are. The ones with the bear painted on the door. Do you?
  > @houses A Haven house near here feeds people. -> houses
  > @careful Stay off the roads at dusk. -> careful
  > @no I don't know where anything is either. -> hub

node houses
  say Feed me. Imagine that. I'll go and look, and if you're lying, I'll never know, will I. I'll just be somewhere else, hungry, thinking well of you.
  > @back1 Let me ask you something else. -> hub

node careful
  say Dusk's when they come out, isn't it. Everybody says it like it's news. It's the only news anyone's sure of any more.
  > @back2 Let me ask you something else. -> hub

conv stranger.tin.girl
for stranger:tin
topic "Tell me about your girl."
prio world
once
voice plain

node start
  say Eleven. Clever. Eats like a sparrow, which is lucky, the way things are at {their:house}. Half portions, and she gives half of hers to the little ones when she thinks I'm not looking.
  say Her mother's on the list for the next walk out. Don't ask me what that means. I don't ask. Nobody at the house asks.
  > @lie She'll be all right. -> fine
  > @nurse Is she eating at all? Coughing? -> nurse   if bg:nurse,doctor
  > @back Let me ask you something else. -> hub

node fine
  say Everyone says that. I've started saying it too, to her, at night. It helps, a bit. Mostly it helps me.
  > @back1 Let me ask you something else. -> hub

node nurse
  say A bit of a cough. Mornings, mostly. You think it's nothing? You'd say if it wasn't. You've got that face, the one the nurse at the house has.
  > @nothing Probably nothing. Keep her warm. -> fine
  > @back2 Let me ask you something else. -> hub

conv stranger.funeral.wife
for stranger:funeral
topic "Tell me about your wife."
prio world
once
voice plain

node start
  say Thursdays to {their:town}, for the market. Thirty years. The car knew the way better than she did. She'd let go of the wheel at the bend by the church to show me.
  say She'd hate this. Standing about on a verge, talking to a stranger. She'd have told you her life story by now, and yours.
  > @tell Tell me about her, then. -> tell
  > @sorry I'm sorry for your loss. -> sorry

node tell
  say She grew marrows the size of dogs and gave them away to people who didn't want them. She cheated at cards and denied it to the end. That's most of her. The rest is mine.
  > @back1 Let me ask you something else. -> hub

node sorry
  say So am I. Help me put the car in the ditch, out of the road, and we'll call it even. She'd hate it blocking the way. She hated being in anyone's way.
  > @back2 Let me ask you something else. -> hub

conv stranger.which_way.pram
for stranger:which_way
topic "Why the pram full of pans?"
prio flavour
once
voice plain

node start
  say It carries more than a bag does, and it's got wheels. Don't look at me like that. Everyone looks at me like that, and then they ask about the baby. There isn't one. It was my neighbour's pram.
  > @fair It's a good idea, actually. -> fair
  > @back Let me ask you something else. -> hub

node fair
  say Thank you. Somebody gets it. The pans are for {their:town}. The house there has none left, apparently. Forty people and two saucepans. Nobody ever thinks of pans.
  > @back1 Let me ask you something else. -> hub

conv stranger.door.tuesday
for stranger:door
topic "How long have you been in there?"
prio world
once
voice plain

node start
  say Since Tuesday. I counted the tins, so it's Tuesday. Unless I counted wrong, and then it's worse.
  say They come out in the street when it's dark. I hear them on the stairs some nights. I don't open the door to anyone after the light goes. Not even you, if you come back.
  > @out It's safe enough to come out. By day. -> out
  > @which Which Tuesday? -> which

node out
  say By day. Everyone says by day. All right. Give me a minute to remember how a door works, and where I put my shoes.
  > @back1 Let me ask you something else. -> hub

node which
  say Don't. Don't do that. I'll start counting again, and I've only just stopped.
  > @back2 Sorry. Let me ask you something else. -> hub

conv stranger.two_in_back.kids
for stranger:two_in_back
topic "Where are you two off to, then?"
prio flavour
once
voice plain

node start
  say Go on, tell them. On an adventure. Isn't that right? An adventure to Gran's, in a car that won't start. The very best kind.
  say (the little one) We're going on an adventure. Dad said.
  > @play Best adventure there is. -> play
  > @plain What about you? Where are you going? -> plain

node play
  say Hear that? Best adventure there is. Thank you. The little one's beaming. The big one's looking at you like you've joined the conspiracy. Which you have.
  > @back1 Let me ask you something else. -> hub

node plain
  say (the older one) We're going to Gran's. Gran's dead. Dad doesn't know I know.
  say What was that? Never mind. Get your head down, both of you. We'll be moving soon.
  > @back2 Let me ask you something else. -> hub

conv stranger.digger.name
for stranger:digger
topic "Who are you burying?"
prio world
once
voice plain

node start
  say It's for {their:who}. I didn't know them. Somebody should, for a minute, before the ground does. Nobody should lie by a road.
  > @help Hand me the shovel. -> help
  > @why Why bother, for a stranger? -> why

node help
  say Thank you. The shovel's worse than the digging. It's a coal shovel from my own shed. Coal shovels aren't made for this. Nothing is.
  > @back1 Let me ask you something else. -> hub

node why
  say Because next time it's me by the road. I'd like someone to bother. That's all it is. It isn't kindness. It's a sort of deposit.
  > @back2 Let me ask you something else. -> hub

conv stranger.still_walking.sleeve
for stranger:still_walking
topic "What happened to your arm?"
prio world
once
voice plain

node start
  say It's nothing. A dog bit me, years ago, before all this. An old scar.
  say That's what I told the house, anyway. They walked me out all the same. Polite about it. A coat, a tin, and a finger pointing at the road.
  > @doctor Show me. I'll know if it's old. -> doctor   if bg:doctor,nurse
  > @leave I won't ask again. -> hub

node doctor
  say Fine. Look, then. It's new. I know it's new, and you know, and now we both know. So tell me straight: is the shot at the lab true, or isn't it?
  > @honest I don't know. Ask at the lab. -> hub
  > @kind Sit down a minute. Then we'll walk. -> hub

conv stranger.warm_hands.fire
for stranger:warm_hands
topic "Where are you from?"
prio flavour
once
voice plain

node start
  say A Haven house, until last week. Upkeep. They count mouths now, and I couldn't work enough to pay for mine, so I'm paying it out here instead.
  say Don't feel sorry for me. The fire's good. The company's better than I'm used to, and nobody here is counting what I eat.
  > @stay Stay as long as the fire lasts. -> stay
  > @back Let me ask you something else. -> hub

node stay
  say Generous. It's only your fire, though, isn't it. Ha. Sorry. I've forgotten how people talk, after a week of talking to hedges.
  > @back1 Let me ask you something else. -> hub

conv stranger.seed_potatoes.farm
for stranger:seed_potatoes
topic "Tell me about the farm."
prio flavour
once
voice plain

node start
  say Four generations of my family on this land. Then a fortnight, and the sick own it. They stand in the rows out there like they're waiting to be told what to plant.
  say Potatoes don't care who eats them. That's what I keep telling myself. It doesn't help as much as you'd think.
  > @why Why go back for a sack of potatoes? -> seed
  > @back Let me ask you something else. -> hub

node seed
  say Because they're seed potatoes, not eating ones. Put a sack in the ground in spring and you've a field by autumn. Somebody should plant them. A house that's still there in spring.
  > @back1 Let me ask you something else. -> hub

conv stranger.sister.barns
for stranger:sister
topic "Tell me about your sister."
prio world
once
voice plain

node start
  say Older than me. Bossier than me. Put out of {their:house} for upkeep, and she'd paid it twice before they asked a third time.
  say She'll be in a barn. {their:barn}, if I had to bet. She liked barns when we were kids. She'd hide in the hay and I'd pretend I couldn't find her.
  > @help I'll keep an eye out for her. -> help
  > @back Let me ask you something else. -> hub

node help
  say That's all I ask. That, and if she says I'm useless, don't argue. She's not wrong.
  > @back1 Let me ask you something else. -> hub

conv stranger.waves_at_line.him
for stranger:waves_at_line
topic "Who are you waving at?"
prio world
once
voice plain

node start
  say My husband. He went for bread on Day 1, over the hill to the town outside, and the road shut behind him. He's there most evenings, past the trees.
  say We wave. That's the arrangement. The drones don't mind waving. The loudspeaker says step back, and I do, one step, and then I wave again.
  > @gently Come back from the line. Please. -> gently
  > @wave I'll wave with you a while. -> wave

node gently
  say In a minute. He hasn't waved yet. He always waves. If I go before he waves, he'll think something's happened to me.
  > @back1 Let me ask you something else. -> hub

node wave
  say There. By the third tree. Did you see that? Something moved. That's him. He'll think I've made a friend. He'll be pleased. He always said I should talk to people more.
  > @back2 Let me ask you something else. -> hub

conv stranger.face_on_notice.book
for stranger:face_on_notice
topic "What do you owe them?"
prio world
once
voice plain

node start
  say Rent. Then interest on the rent. Then a fee for being late with the interest. It's all in the landlord's book, in the crew hut at {their:hut}. Page after page of me.
  say The landlord wears the red hand now. The book's the only thing in the Zone that still works the way it used to.
  > @why Why come to me with it? -> why
  > @back Let me ask you something else. -> hub

node why
  say Because you're on a notice. A face the crews want gone. Somebody with nothing left to lose doesn't worry about a crew hut. I've plenty to lose, and all of it's on those pages.
  > @back1 Let me ask you something else. -> hub

conv stranger.hook_hiding.noise
for stranger:hook_hiding
topic "What did you see out there?"
prio world
once
voice plain

node start
  say Nothing. I heard all of it and saw nothing. The shooting, the shouting, then the other noise. I put my hands over my ears like a child and stayed under here.
  > @fine That kept you alive. -> fine
  > @back Let me ask you something else. -> hub

node fine
  say Did it? Maybe. I'd like to think something did on purpose. It feels like luck, and I'm tired of being kept alive by luck.
  > @back1 Let me ask you something else. -> hub

conv stranger.hook_first.bag
for stranger:hook_first
topic "What did you find?"
prio flavour
once
voice plain

node start
  say Enough. Not as much as I'd like. More than you'd like, by your face. Tins, a torch, a box of plasters. Somebody's whole cupboard.
  say Don't take it personally. Being first is the only luck left going. Tomorrow it'll be you, and I'll be the one standing here with that face.
  > @back Let me ask you something else. -> hub

conv stranger.hook_bitten.fence
for stranger:hook_bitten
topic "How did you get that scratch?"
prio world
once
voice plain

node start
  say A fence. Barbed wire. Off a farm, coming across the fields. You know what a fence looks like. Don't look at it like that.
  > @look Let me look at it. -> look   if bg:doctor,nurse
  > @believe A fence. All right, then. -> hub

node look
  say Go on, then. Look. You've gone quiet. That's the answer, isn't it. Don't say it. Just tell me which way the house is, and whether they'll open the door.
  > @house There's a house near. Go there now. -> hub
  > @sit I'll sit with you a minute first. -> hub

# A stranger calls out as you come close (docs/DIALOGUE.md, "Who opens a conversation"): once, at
# 10 m, inside the unasked-contact budget. What they want is still their ask, as built.
conv stranger.any.callout
for stranger
greet
opens approach 10
prio quest
once
voice plain

node start
  say? !met :: Hey. You. Sorry. Have you got a minute? I wouldn't ask, only there's nobody else on this road, and you look like you know your way about.
